@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ito-rounding-order-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-rounding-order-5746`

-- Tests for the Income Tax (Rules for Rounding Amounts) Order 5746-1986, ss 1-17.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the Order's own rule (limb (a): the round amount is
-- a multiple of the step; limb (b): below half a step the excess is dropped, from half a step the
-- step is added) BEFORE the assertion was run. The arithmetic is written beside each group.
-- A failing assertion here is a finding, never a value to edit.
-- The adjusted amounts are HYPOTHETICAL unless a comment says the figure is printed in the
-- Ordinance (301,200 and 560,280 in s 121 are).

§ `Tests of the Rounding Order`

§§ `Order s 1 — income ceilings, step 120`
-- 301,259 = 120 x 2,510 + 59   (120 x 2,510 = 301,200): excess 59 < 60, dropped  -> 301,200
-- 301,260 = 301,200 + 60: excess 60, not less than 60, a step is added            -> 301,320
-- 301,200 is a multiple: excess 0                                                  -> 301,200
-- 1,139.9 = 120 x 9 + 59.9 (1,080 + 59.9): excess 59.9 < 60                       -> 1,080
-- 1,140   = 1,080 + 60                                                             -> 1,200
-- 1,199.99 = 1,080 + 119.99                                                        -> 1,200
-- 0 -> 0
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 301_259 EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 301_260 EQUALS 301_320
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 301_200 EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 1139.9 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 1140 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 1199.99 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 0 EQUALS 0
-- 560,280 = 120 x 4,669 (120 x 4,669 = 560,280): a multiple                       -> 560,280
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 560_280 EQUALS 560_280
-- A negative adjusted amount is outside the Order.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` (0 MINUS 1) BECAUSE "the Rounding Order rounds adjusted amounts, and says nothing of a negative one"

§§ `Order s 2 — credit points, step 12`
-- 125   = 12 x 10 + 5: excess 5 < 6                                                -> 120
-- 126   = 120 + 6: excess 6                                                        -> 132
-- 131.99 = 120 + 11.99                                                             -> 132
-- 120 -> 120
-- 2,904 = 12 x 242 -> 2,904
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 125 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 126 EQUALS 132
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 131.99 EQUALS 132
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 2904 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 5.99 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Order s 2 — round the amount of credit points` 6 EQUALS 12

§§ `Order s 3 — allowance points, the nearest whole new shekel`
-- 235.49: round amount 235, excess 0.49 < 0.5 -> 235
-- 235.5:  excess 0.5, half a shekel counts as a shekel -> 236
-- 235.6 -> 236 ; 242 -> 242 ; 0.4 -> 0 ; 0.5 -> 1
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 235.49 EQUALS 235
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 235.5 EQUALS 236
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 235.6 EQUALS 236
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 242 EQUALS 242
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 0.4 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Order s 3 — round the amount of allowance points` 0.5 EQUALS 1

§§ `Order s 4 — the exemption of section 9(5)(a), step 1,200`
-- 12,599 = 1,200 x 10 + 599 = 12,000 + 599: excess 599 < 600 -> 12,000
-- 12,600 = 12,000 + 600 -> 13,200
-- 13,200 is a multiple -> 13,200
#ASSERT `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` 12_599 EQUALS 12_000
#ASSERT `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` 12_600 EQUALS 13_200
#ASSERT `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` 13_200 EQUALS 13_200
#ASSERT `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` 599.99 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Order s 4 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(a)` 600 EQUALS 1200

§§ `Order s 5 — the exemption of section 9(5)(b), step 120`
-- same as s 1: 1,139.9 -> 1,080 ; 1,140 -> 1,200 ; 59.9 -> 0 ; 60 -> 120
#ASSERT `Order s 5 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(b)` 1139.9 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `Order s 5 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(b)` 1140 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `Order s 5 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(b)` 59.9 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Order s 5 — round the exemption of section 9(5)(b)` 60 EQUALS 120

§§ `Order s 6 — a retirement or death grant, step 10`
-- 104.99 = 100 + 4.99 < 5 -> 100 ; 105 = 100 + 5 -> 110 ; 110 -> 110 ; 4.99 -> 0 ; 5 -> 10
#ASSERT `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` 104.99 EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` 105 EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` 110 EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` 4.99 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `Order s 6 — round a retirement grant or a death grant` 5 EQUALS 10

§§ `Order s 7 — the discounts an employee receives, step 12`
-- 17.99 = 12 + 5.99 < 6 -> 12 ; 18 = 12 + 6 -> 24 ; 24 -> 24
#ASSERT `Order s 7 — round the discounts an employee receives` 17.99 EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `Order s 7 — round the discounts an employee receives` 18 EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `Order s 7 — round the discounts an employee receives` 24 EQUALS 24

§§ `Order s 8 — a qualifying annuity, step 10`
-- 9,994.99 = 9,990 + 4.99 -> 9,990 ; 9,995 = 9,990 + 5 -> 10,000
#ASSERT `Order s 8 — round a qualifying annuity` 9994.99 EQUALS 9990
#ASSERT `Order s 8 — round a qualifying annuity` 9995 EQUALS 10_000

§§ `Order s 9 — the exempt amount, the nearest new shekel`
-- 5,000.49 -> 5,000 ; 5,000.5 -> 5,001
#ASSERT `Order s 9 — round the exempt amount` 5000.49 EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT `Order s 9 — round the exempt amount` 5000.5 EQUALS 5001

§§ `Order s 10 — the ceiling for medical-expenses credit, step 120`
-- 22,859.99 = 120 x 190 + 59.99 (22,800 + 59.99) -> 22,800 ; 22,860 = 22,800 + 60 -> 22,920
#ASSERT `Order s 10 — round the ceiling for medical expenses` 22859.99 EQUALS 22_800
#ASSERT `Order s 10 — round the ceiling for medical expenses` 22860 EQUALS 22_920

§§ `Order s 11 — the amount for credit, step 12`
-- 1,205.99 = 12 x 100 + 5.99 (1,200 + 5.99) -> 1,200 ; 1,206 -> 1,212
#ASSERT `Order s 11 — round the amount for credit` 1205.99 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `Order s 11 — round the amount for credit` 1206 EQUALS 1212

§§ `Order s 12 — qualifying income, step 1,200`
-- 100,000 = 1,200 x 83 + 400 (99,600 + 400): 400 < 600 -> 99,600
-- 100,200 = 99,600 + 600 -> 100,800
#ASSERT `Order s 12 — round qualifying income` 100_000 EQUALS 99_600
#ASSERT `Order s 12 — round qualifying income` 100_200 EQUALS 100_800
#ASSERT `Order s 12 — round qualifying income` 100_199.99 EQUALS 99_600

§§ `Order s 13 — the fine under s 188, step 10`
-- 1,234 = 1,230 + 4 -> 1,230 ; 1,235 -> 1,240
#ASSERT `Order s 13 — round the fine` 1234 EQUALS 1230
#ASSERT `Order s 13 — round the fine` 1235 EQUALS 1240

§§ `Order s 15 — the next adjustment starts from the unrounded amount`
-- 1,139.9 rounds (s 1) to 1,080, and the base of the next adjustment stays 1,139.9.
#ASSERT `Order s 1 — round an income ceiling` 1139.9 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `Order s 15 — the amount the next adjustment under section 120B starts from` 1139.9 `, the rounded figure being` 1080 EQUALS 1139.9

§§ `Order s 17 — commencement on 1 January 1986`
#ASSERT `Order s 17 — the Order is in force on` (YMD 1986 1 1)
#ASSERT `Order s 17 — the Order is in force on` (YMD 2026 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Order s 17 — the Order is in force on` (YMD 1985 12 31)

§§ `Which section of the Order rounds which kind of amount`
-- Kind -> step: 301,259 is a multiple of 120 plus 59 -> 301,200 as an income ceiling.
-- The same 125 as a credit point (step 12) is 120, and as an allowance point (step 1) is 125.
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 301_259 `as an amount of the kind` `an income ceiling` EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 125 `as an amount of the kind` `the amount of a credit point` EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 125 `as an amount of the kind` `the amount of an allowance point` EQUALS 125
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 12_600 `as an amount of the kind` `the exemption of a blind or 100% disabled person, section 9(5)(a)` EQUALS 13_200
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1140 `as an amount of the kind` `the exemption of a blind or disabled person not from personal exertion, section 9(5)(b)` EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 105 `as an amount of the kind` `a retirement grant or death grant, sections 9(7A) and 32(9)(a)(1)` EQUALS 110
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 18 `as an amount of the kind` `the discount an employee receives from the employer, section 9(20)` EQUALS 24
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 9995 `as an amount of the kind` `a qualifying annuity, section 9A(a) and (c)` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 5000.5 `as an amount of the kind` `the exempt amount, section 9A(b)` EQUALS 5001
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 22_860 `as an amount of the kind` `the ceiling for medical-expenses credit, section 44(a)(1)` EQUALS 22_920
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1206 `as an amount of the kind` `the amount for credit, section 45A(d)` EQUALS 1212
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 100_200 `as an amount of the kind` `qualifying income, section 47` EQUALS 100_800
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1235 `as an amount of the kind` `a fine for failing to file a report, section 188` EQUALS 1240

§§ `Fork R1 — an amount the Order names no rule for`
-- By default (declined), whatever the amount, even one that is already a multiple of every step.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `an amount in section 9(16A), (16B) or (18A)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `the amount in section 17(5A)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `an amount in section 32(9) other than the grant of paragraph (a)(1)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `an amount in section 45A other than subsection (d)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `the amount in section 58A(c)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `an amount in section 125D` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1200 `as an amount of the kind` `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
-- The other reading, by name: the amount stays as the index adjustment left it (1,139.9 stays 1,139.9).
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1139.9 `as an amount of the kind` `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)` `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` `such an amount stays as adjusted` EQUALS 1139.9
#ASSERT REFUSED `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 1139.9 `as an amount of the kind` `a recognised donation amount, section 46(a)` `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` `the rounding of such an amount is declined` BECAUSE "the Rounding Order has no rule for this amount, and section 120B(d) does not say what it is rounded to"
-- The readings do not part on an amount the Order DOES name: the switch is not read there.
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 301_259 `as an amount of the kind` `an income ceiling` `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` `such an amount stays as adjusted` EQUALS 301_200
#ASSERT `the Order rounds the adjusted amount` 301_259 `as an amount of the kind` `an income ceiling` `, reading an amount it has no rule for as` `the rounding of such an amount is declined` EQUALS 301_200

§§ `Limb (a) read as "the nearest", limb (b) read after it: the same figure in every case (step 120)`
-- Hand-worked in steps of 120; the floor reading, the nearest-tie-down reading and the nearest-tie-up
-- reading each give the figure on the right.
--   0 -> 0 ; 59.99 -> 0 ; 60 -> 120 ; 60.01 -> 120 ; 119.99 -> 120 ; 120 -> 120 ; 179.99 -> 120 ; 180 -> 240
--   1,139.9 -> 1,080 ; 1,140 -> 1,200
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 0 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 59.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 60 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 60.01 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 119.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 120 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 179.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `the Order rounds` 180 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 0 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 59.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 60 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 60.01 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 119.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 120 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 179.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 180 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 1139.9 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going down, then (b):` 1140 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 1200
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 0 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 59.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 60 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 60.01 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 119.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 120 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 179.99 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 120
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 180 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 240
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 1139.9 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 1080
#ASSERT `reading (a) as the nearest multiple, a tie going up, then (b):` 1140 `in steps of` 120 EQUALS 1200
